It's amazing how every time ABA launches a new title about making websites it feels like *an event*, one that smart people worth paying attention to are genuinely excited about. Erin Kissane's *Elements of Content Strategy* is (naturally) less about code than the HTML5 and CSS3 books preceding it, but no less succinct, clear, practical and great.

#### Related:

-   [Read an excerpt from *The Elements of Content Strategy*, "A Checklist for Content Work," in this week's issue of *A List Apart*.](http://www.alistapart.com/articles/a-checklist-for-content-work/)
-   [Erin Kissane's blog post announcing the book's release.](http://incisive.nu/2011/now-out-the-elements-of-content-strategy/)
